190:{character:player}What choice did you make?
191:{character:Ju}Me? Haha, of course I chose to move to the right. This way, everyone has a bright future. Isn't that great?
192:{character:player}I don't know the model answer to this question, but I know it isn't right to choose the left or the right.
193:{character:player}We can't actively hurt others just because our own interests are threatened. No one has the right to decide the fate of others.
194:{character:Ju}Haha, aren't the interests of the young people on the train important? Because of your hesitation, they have lost their lives, dreams, and futures. Haven't you also unilaterally decided their fate?
195:{character:player}I haven't given up on them. Although trying to save everyone looks unrealistic, that alone shouldn't stop us from aiming to achieve this objective.
196:{character:player}There are many things we can do before the train hits the track and derails, such as slowing down the train, trying to stop it, asking for help, or getting others to save the people on the tracks... We can always find a glimmer of opportunity.
197:{character:player}It's too cruel to give up on someone else's life without trying to do anything.
