200:After a while, he stands and rubs his eyes with his hands before he looks at me.
201:{character:Ju}You're too funny. You made me laugh so hard I started crying.
202:{character:Ju}Well, do you think you're Soul's opportunity?
203:{character:player}I... I don't know, but I'm willing to try my best.
204:Clap--Clap--Clap-- He claps three times crisply, then pulls out another envelope from his inside pocket as an afterthought and hands it to me. It's almost as if a blue robotic cat's dimensional pocket is hidden under his plain-looking jacket.
205:{character:Ju}I can't wait to see what opportunities you'll bring to Soul then.
210:{character:Ciri}Since Ju has told you the general situation of what happened back then, I'll tell you the whole story so you don't have any wild thoughts.
212:{character:Ciri}Ju and I were both adopted by Sid, the second-generation leader of Soul when we were children. Unlike Sara, who grew up in a rich family and joined Soul because she loved dancing, we had been touring everywhere with the troupe since we were young, and we were used to the fickleness of human nature.
214:{character:Ciri}Sid and Sara were both born into wealthy families and received similar educations since they were young, so they had a similar outlook on things. That's why Sid chose Sara to be the third-generation leader of Soul instead of Ju, who had always been working hard to become Sid's successor. In his eyes, Sid was favoring Sara over him.
215:{character:Ciri}As you know, Soul used to travel throughout the world when performing on tour, and the group has had a practice of taking in people who had no home to return to since the first-generation leader led the group. After spending so much time together, we became more like family than colleagues.
216:{character:Ciri}This kind of relationship has both advantages and disadvantages. One disadvantage is that Soul now has a large number of old, feeble, sick, and sometimes disabled people who contribute little to the group, which has made our finances increasingly tight... By the time Sara took over as leader, we were already struggling to make ends meet, and we mostly performed to make a living.
217:{character:Ciri}Ju noticed this problem a long time ago. He believed that it would be better to deal with the problem once and for all no matter how painful it would be rather than prolong the agony. Instead of letting these people become a burden to Soul, he wanted to make them leave Soul and find their own way to survive.
218:{character:Ciri}Sara regards Soul as her home, and the members as her family. She believed that only they themselves could decide whether they would leave or stay, and not even the leader could make that decision for them.
220:{character:player}What about you?
221:{character:Ciri}Me?
222:{character:player}Didn't you want to become the leader?
223:{character:Ciri}I'm used to being a loner. The position of leader is a burden to me.
224:{character:player}What do you think about Ju and Sara's disagreement?
225:{character:Ciri}Actually, wild beasts often choose to abandon the old, feeble, sick, and disabled to preserve the rest of the population. This isn't anything strange in nature, so I won't judge whether Ju or Sara is right or wrong. They are both trying to protect Soul in different ways, and even I have my own way of protecting Soul.
226:{character:Ciri}I have chosen to stay with Sara because my intuition tells me that Sara is able to give Soul a brighter future.
227:{character:Ciri}Okay, that's the end of the story. {var:player_nickname}, you've always been a person who has strong opinions, so I won't ask you to side with any of us. You just need to continue doing what you think is right.
228:{character:player}Hmm, yeah.
229:Neither Ciri nor I pursue this topic further. Instead, we open the envelope Ju gave me after a moment of silence and find a hand-drawn map inside it. Based on the feeling of familiarity I get from this soul painting, I believe Ju drew this himself.
230:As the street name is marked, it's easy to tell that the destination is a club in the east side of the city. In fact, it's only a few streets away from the Raven hideout we visited yesterday.
231:Ciri and I exchange a glance and decide to show Soumu this map.
232:By the time we arrive at the Raven hideout, it is already well past the time we agreed to meet Soumu. On the way there, my quick-witted brain works furiously to think of an explanation for our lateness.
233:After thinking about it, I decide that the best solution is to show him the map and tell him we've found a suspicious place.
234:However, the scene in front of the hideout is not what I expected at all. There are two groups of people confronting each other on both sides of the street, and the tension is so thick that no pedestrians dare to pass through them.
235:Fortunately, this street isn't a main road, or else each person would be fined 5,000 Coppers for obstructing traffic.
236:Shijukara sees us from a distance and quickly calls for us to go over to him and stand behind Soumu together. Speaking in a low voice, I ask him what is going on while Ciri stares at the other side with a serious look on her face.
237:{character:player}What's going on?
238:Shijukara
239:{character:Shijukara}The people standing opposite us are from Strix based in the west side of the city, and they've always been at odds with us. They are just a gang of barbaric information dealers though, so you don't need to be scared.
240:{character:player}Why have they come here today? Are they here to fight you? Is this a gang fight?
242:{character:player}Did your boss accept?
243:{character:Shijukara}Of course not. That's why we're all stuck here.
244:{character:player}Oh, so even you know that the situation is very tense.
245:{character:Shijukara}Nonsense! I'm not stupid.
246:If this is the reason... I think for a moment, then I take the map out of my pocket and hand it to Soumu.
247:{character:player}Aniki, please take a look at this. I've found a suspicious location.
248:I didn't really expect that this excuse would come in handy. I'm so smart.
249:The young man wearing a hat at the very front of the people across the street looks at me with interest and suddenly starts speaking.
250:{character:???}{var:player_nickname}.
251:I'm a little surprised when he calls out my name from the other side of the street, but what surprises me even more is that Shijukara also looks at me with a shocked expression, as if he had only just learned my name.
252:Slightly confused, I turn to look at the young man.
253:{character:player}You know who I am?
254:{character:???}Of course.
255:The man laughs and claps his hands to tell everyone to be quiet. After that, he speaks in a loud voice.
256:{character:???}Listen up, everyone. The person standing in front of you is "the famous guardian of Mahjong Soul Shrine's priestess, the best friend of students of Asaha High School, a core non-staff member of Soul, an esteemed guest of Samu Corporation, Kazuha Saionji's only disciple, an honorary customer of Éternité, the senpai who is a confidant of Aotsuyu Middle School, and the leader of the children of Central Park..."
257:Whoa, I didn't expect the prefix to my name to be so long. It makes me feel kinda embarrassed, but yes, that's me. Keep going because I love to hear it.
258:Soumu
259:{character:Soumu}You can leave now.
260:Soumu, who had just finished reading the map, seems unable to understand the lively atmosphere and interrupts the person's words. What a shame. There are still many prefixes to my name that can be shared with everyone.
261:Soumu waves the map in his hand at the other side. His tone is three parts of ridicule, four parts of disdain, two parts of indifference, and one part of smugness. In short, I can tell from his tone that he really hates the young man on the other side.
262:{character:Soumu}You want to exchange such a common piece of information for a favor from me? Kutsuji, you seem to be regressing as you age.
263:The other person ignores his words and looks at me instead.
264:Kutsuji
265:{character:Kutsuji}Since he's already said everything, I won't bother to introduce myself.
266:{character:Kutsuji}{var:player_nickname}, do you know that you can also ask me to help you? I can do whatever Soumu can do and even do what Soumu can't.
267:{character:Kutsuji}Well, think about it. Do you want me to help you take care of everything else?
268:After he speaks, I can feel everyone's eyes on me, especially the eyes of Soumu, who is only 30 centimeters away from me. His fierce gaze and tight muscles on his forearms tell me one thing, that is, he will tear me in half if I dare to nod.
269:In this situation, of course I'll choose to stay with Raven. Besides, I don't know the person on the other side. No matter how I look at it, he doesn't really want to help me. He just wants to use me as a weapon in his fight with Soumu.
270:{character:player}Sorry, I've already agreed to work with Raven.
271:The people around me become excited after I tactfully reject the other person. The guy with slicked back hair and the guy with side part hair, who were playing mahjong with Soumu last time, are unable to contain their excitement and rush to the middle of the road.
272:Guy with Slicked Back Hair
273:{character:Guy with Slicked Back Hair}Hey, why are you guys from Strix still here?
274:Guy with Side Part Hair
275:{character:Guy with Side Part Hair}Our boss told you to get lost.
276:{character:Guy with Slicked Back Hair}Well? Why haven't you left yet? Are you looking for a fight? Bring it on then. We're not afraid of you!
277:I begin to worry that they really will start fighting, but Shijukara seems to know what I'm thinking and comes over to comfort me.
279:I can see Soumu take a deep sigh beside me. Shijukara really needs to learn to be more astute.
280:Soumu pats my shoulder and motions for me to have a talk with him inside.
281:On our way to the room, I remember the shocked expression that Shijukara made when he heard my name earlier. This is the perfect timing to ask him about it.
282:{character:player}When you guys talk about me and Ciri, what do you usually call me?
284:{character:player}You rely on these two common nicknames to identify us?
286:{character:player}Oh, well I know your real name now, Shijukawa.
287:{character:Shijukara}... ¥%……&&*!
288:After a moment of stunned silence, Shijukara starts swearing.
289:Kids these days. How can they just reveal your real name when you have a nickname. You have no safety awareness at all.
290:There's no one in the mahjong dojo today, probably because they were scared away by the big scene at the door just now. Soumu walks over to a sofa and sits down casually.
291:{character:Soumu}Sit wherever you want.
292:{character:player}Oh, sure.
293:{character:Ciri}Thanks.
294:{character:Soumu}I know the place on that map.
295:{character:player}Oh?
296:{character:Soumu}When my men only found bits and pieces of information after searching all day, I guessed that this incident might be related to those people.
297:{character:Ciri}Who are you talking about?
298:{character:Soumu}Yu.
299:{character:player}Yu?
300:{character:Soumu}Look carefully at the map.
301:Ciri and I take the map Soumu hands back to us and look at it carefully. On the map, we see that the word "Yu" has been circled in red next to the name of the club. However, because Ju's handwriting is so illegible that we mistook it for a simple pattern.
302:{character:Soumu}Yu is the largest and most mysterious organization in One Han City, and its scope of influence exceeds your wildest imagination. It's because this organization is protecting this wildlife trafficking organization that it has been able to run wild in my territory for so long without being caught, hmph.
303:{character:Soumu}I don't know where you got this piece of information from, but judging from the information we found, I'm pretty sure it's true.
304:{character:player}Then will you help us?
305:{character:Soumu}Yes, of course I will. After all, making trouble for Yu is what I like to do the most.
306:Is this the hobby of a gang leader? I don't understand it at all. Although I'm shocked, I think it's a good thing that he's willing to help us.
307:{character:Soumu}However, we probably won't be able to save those animals today. According to our experiences in past dealings with them, they should be guarding the animals heavily right now. If we break in forcefully, they might destroy the evidence.
308:{character:player}What do you mean by "destroy the evidence"?
309:{character:Soumu}For example... they might burn down the warehouse. Do you understand what I'm saying?
310:{character:player}I understand. When would be a good time to go?
311:Soumu doesn't answer my question. Instead, he shouts at someone outside.
312:{character:Soumu}Ryou.
313:{character:Guy with Slicked Back Hair}Boss, you called for me?
314:Ther guy with slicked back hair who was arguing outside came back at some point and has been standing outside the door.
315:{character:Soumu}Tell them what you found out.
316:{character:Guy with Slicked Back Hair}Yes. Our brothers learned that a warehouse in the east side of the city was very noisy last night. When they went there, they saw that it was extremely tightly guarded. When this happens, it usually means something fishy is going on, so they staked out the place for a while.
317:{character:Guy with Slicked Back Hair}After that, we learned that they change shifts at eight in the morning. This is also when things get more chaotic and their defenses become weaker.
318:{character:Soumu}The warehouse they found is behind the club on the map. Tomorrow morning, I'll send some men to go there with you.
319:After hearing him say that he'll send some men to go with us, I look at Shijukara next to me. After all, we got to know each other pretty well after our fight and even learned each other's real names. We can almost be considered old friends now.
320:{character:Soumu}Not this piece of trash.
321:{character:player}Huh?
322:Soumu looks at someone in the corner, then a young boy who looks really thin stands up in the corner.
323:{character:Soumu}This kid is called Oumu, and his greatest skill is lock picking. There's no lock in One Han City that he can't open.
324:{character:Soumu}Tomorrow morning, you'll sneak in with Oumu when they change shifts. After that, Shijukara will sow confusion outside to divert their attention.
325:{character:Soumu}Once you find the animals you want to take with you, send us a message, and someone will pick you up outside.
326:The plan sounds simple, but if you think about it carefully, you'll realize that the process is not simple at all, and things can go wrong at every step. Soumu doesn't seem to have considered that an ordinary, harmless, and kind citizen like me might not have certain abilities.
327:Ciri pats my shoulder, and her warm palm calms me down a little. Fortunately, I still have an amazing teammate with me.
328:I'll let Ciri and the people from Raven work out the details of the action we'll take later. Unlike me, she seems to be a natural at this type of thing.
329:Heroine, how do you manage to switch between being a heroine and a banditess so easily?
330:On my way home from Raven, I meet a girl whose coat collar is turned up so high that it covers half her face. She walks up to me and hands me a note without saying anything, then she leaves.
331:Why is everyone using paper notes today? What's so special about it today?
333:I really want to show Ju this so he will know how important it is to have good handwriting.
334:I don't know who wrote this note. Maybe this is a friendly reminder with good intentions, but this one sentence isn't enough for me to find out if there is any deeper meaning. After all, I had only heard about the organization called Yu today.
336:Go with Nadeshiko.
